      "content": "Thank you. Regarding step 2 (Data Analysis), I have a specific concern. The variances are remarkably small—often between 2 and 8 Euros—and they don't follow a predictable cadence. It's almost as if these tiny amounts are just being scavenged or nipped away from the total in a way that evades standard threshold alerts. \n\nGiven the 'nuisance' nature of these small, irregular scraps of budget being depleted, how would you refine the Data Analysis or Anomaly Detection step to catch these specific types of micro-discrepancies without triggering a massive false-positive rate in our automated monitoring systems?",
